# File: tests/bdd/features/generate_audio_node_types.feature
# Generated from: specs/285-guard-every-elevenlabs-audio-node-type-with-the-one-take-rule/requirements.md
Feature: Guard every ElevenLabs audio node type with the one-take rule

  @SCN001
  Scenario Outline: A multi-take call for any audio node type is denied
    Given an empty hook state directory
    When the audio guard hook receives a creative_generate_in_flow event with node_type "<node_type>" and no generations_count for session "s-1"
    Then it exits 0
    And its permissionDecision is "deny"
    And its permissionDecisionReason states generations_count: 1 and names /generate-audio

    Examples:
      | node_type      |
      | tts            |
      | sfx            |
      | music          |
      | dubbing-audio  |
      | voice-changer  |
      | voice-isolator |
      | audio-effects  |
      | video-to-music |
      | composition    |

  @SCN002
  Scenario: The guarded set matches the MCP's audio-output node types
    Given the recorded ElevenLabs node-type list in tests/fixtures/elevenlabs/flow_node_types.json
    When the audio node types are derived as every audio-output type plus composition
    Then they equal the guard hook's AUDIO_NODE_TYPES
    And docs/mcp/elevenlabs.md lists exactly those node types

  @SCN003
  Scenario Outline: Non-audio node types are left alone
    Given an empty hook state directory
    When the audio guard hook receives a creative_generate_in_flow event with node_type "<node_type>" and generations_count 4 for session "s-1"
    Then it exits 0 with empty stdout
    And no reminder marker is written

    Examples:
      | node_type        |
      | image-generation |
      | video-generation |
      | dubbing-video    |
      | voice-creation   |

  @SCN004
  Scenario: The skill and the doc name every guarded audio node type
    Given the bodies of skills/generate-audio/SKILL.md and docs/mcp/elevenlabs.md
    When they are read
    Then each names every node type in the guard hook's AUDIO_NODE_TYPES
    And each states generations_count: 1
